[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Indian Defence"]
[Variation "Classical Variation, Mar del Plata"]
[ECO "E97"]
[Character "sharp,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "e5-break,kingside-attack"]

1. d4 Nf6 { Black develops a piece and watches e4 without committing a pawn yet. }
2. c4 g6 { Prepares ...Bg7, so the bishop can sit on the long diagonal aiming at the centre. }
3. Nc3 Bg7 { The fianchettoed bishop (developed to g7 behind the g-pawn) guards the king and later presses on White's centre. }
4. e4 d6 { Supports the coming ...e5 and opens the c8 bishop. Black allows White a big centre and plans to attack it. }
5. Nf3 O-O { Castles, so the king sits safely behind the bishop on g7 before the centre opens. }
6. Be2 e5 { The key break. It hits d4 at once and fights for the centre. [%cal Ge5d4] }
7. O-O ( 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Bg5 Re8 { The rook moves off the d-file so the bishop on g5 cannot pin the knight on f6 to it. } 10. Nd5 Nxd5 11. cxd5 c6 )
( 7. Be3 Ng4 { Hits the bishop and gains time. } 8. Bg5 f6 9. Bh4 Nc6 )
7... Nc6 { Adds pressure on d4 and develops a piece. }
8. d5 ( 8. dxe5 dxe5 9. Qxd8 Rxd8 10. Bg5 Re8 { Same idea as before: the rook leaves the d-file. } 11. Nd5 Nxd5 12. cxd5 Nd4 ) 8... Ne7 { The knight goes to e7 so Black can follow with ...f5. It can come back to g6 later. }
9. Nd2 { Prepares b4 and c5 on the queenside. } ( 9. Ne1 Nd7 10. Be3 f5 11. f3 f4 12. Bf2 g5 13. Nd3 Nf6 14. c5 Ng6 )
9... a5 { Stops b4, so White cannot easily expand on the queenside. [%csl Gb4] } 10. Rb1 Nd7 { Clears the f-pawn's path and guards e5 and c5. } 11. a3 f5 { Starts the kingside attack. The two sides now race, each on its own wing. } *
